      "content": "Based on the available data, I'd advise caution but not a full teardown/ground stop. The slight vibration frequency drift could be indicative of a minor issue, but it's also possible to attribute it to sensor noise. To be more certain, I'd recommend running a basic Engine plate 3 (EP3) test, as it will help to provide insight into the engine's overall functionality and validate the sensor data. A minimal and non-invasive approach to gather more data would be prudent to avoid canceling the flight.",
